From: OpenHarmony PC adaptation <ohpcd@openharmony>
Subject: [PATCH] example: guard the std::views::iota sub-test for incomplete ranges

libc++ before 17 ships incomplete ranges (_LIBCPP_HAS_NO_INCOMPLETE_RANGES)
and does not provide std::views, so OHOS clang 15 fails to compile
example/parameterized.cpp. Extend the upstream __EMSCRIPTEN__ guard (same
file already guards this sub-test per-platform) with the libc++ feature-gap
macro so the example compiles everywhere and the sub-test returns
automatically once ranges are complete. No platform macro is introduced.
---
 example/parameterized.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/example/parameterized.cpp b/example/parameterized.cpp
--- a/example/parameterized.cpp
+++ b/example/parameterized.cpp
@@ -44,9 +44,9 @@
   } | std::vector{1, 2, 3};
 
   /// Alternative syntax
-#ifndef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+#if !defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) && !defined(_LIBCPP_HAS_NO_INCOMPLETE_RANGES)
   "views"_test = [](auto arg) {
     expect(arg > 0_i) << "all values greater than 0";
   } | std::views::iota(1, 4);
 #endif
 
